[
    {
        "content": "<p>This is a proposal to standardize the way we handle commutativity of subobjects (in a noncommutative ambient type).</p>\n<p>Currently, we have a bit of a mishmash in this regard. We have constructors like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Algebra.adjoinCommSemiringOfComm#doc\">docs#Algebra.adjoinCommSemiringOfComm</a> or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Algebra.adjoinCommRingOfComm#doc\">docs#Algebra.adjoinCommRingOfComm</a> to turn the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Algebra.adjoin#doc\">docs#Algebra.adjoin</a> of a set of commuting elements into a <code>Semiring</code> or a <code>Ring</code>, as appropriate; I'll refer to this as the <em>bundled approach</em>. At the same time we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsMulCommutative#doc\">docs#IsMulCommutative</a> as a mixin for saying that a type is commutative, and we even have (unscoped!) instances like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CommMonoid.ofIsMulCommutative#doc\">docs#CommMonoid.ofIsMulCommutative</a> or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CommGroup.ofIsMulCommutative#doc\">docs#CommGroup.ofIsMulCommutative</a> (although I think these are the only two such instances) which build the bundled instance from the unbundled one.</p>\n<p>I propose a hybrid approach to dealing with commutativity of subobjects, which boils down to essentially the following:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Unbundle commutativity for subobjects using <code>IsMulCommutative</code>, and add scoped (to <code>IsMulCommutative</code>) instances which build bundled commutative versions from the unbundled noncommutative versions with <code>IsMulCommutative</code> assumptions.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Here are the considerations that went into this suggestion.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The current bundled approach using things like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Algebra.adjoinCommSemiringOfComm#doc\">docs#Algebra.adjoinCommSemiringOfComm</a> is cumbersome, and causes much duplication (you need one for <code>CommSemiring</code>, <code>CommRing</code>, <code>NormedCommRing</code>, <code>SeminormedCommRing</code>, etc.). With the unbundled approach, these all become a single theorem of the form:</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isMulCommutativeAdjoin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uR</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">uA</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcomm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↥</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">adjoin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Using the unbundled approach, we can also allow type class synthesis to work for us when we're doing things like taking the <code>adjoin</code> of an existing commutative subobject (even of a different type than <code>Subalgebra</code>!), as in the following example. Note that such instances are a bit bad for type class synthesis since Lean sees <code>IsMulCommutative ↥_</code>, so we don't want Lean to go looking for these instances all the time. Many instances that we may write about <code>IsMulCommutative</code> and subobjects suffer from being somewhat bad in this manner, because we always coerce to type.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instIsMulCommutativeAdjoin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SetLike</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MulMemClass</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">adjoin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>In the context of the previous example, we would really like for Lean to be able to conclude automatically <code>CommSemiring ↥(adjoin R (s : Set A))</code> so that we don't have to write it manually. So we add the instance:</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- A semiring with commutative multiplication is a commutative semiring. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">priority</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">50</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li>\n<p>We mark this with <code>priority := 50</code> so that it is very low on the list of things to try, but we also scope it to the <code>IsMulCommutative</code> namespace. This means that we can isolate the unbundled approach, along with the relatively bad <code>IsMulCommutative</code> instances, from the rest of the library, which is bundled. That way, people can open this scope when they need to work with commutative subobjects. Of course, the downside to this approach is always discoverability of the scope. We can improve this by adding the information to docstrings and adding a library note.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>We can have other nice instances, such as, for example:</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subalgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isMulCommutative_iSup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Preorder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsDirectedOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">o</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subalgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⨆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subalgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subalgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instIsMulCommutativeTopologicalClosure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">TopologicalSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsTopologicalSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">T2Space</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subalgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">topologicalClosure</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>cc: <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"477483\">@Monica Omar</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"462733\">@Jon Bannon</span></p>",
